# {{name}}

{{description}}

A Sophon document extractor plugin that extracts text from custom file
formats for the document processing pipeline.

## Implemented Interface

`IDocumentExtractor` from `Sophon.Plugin.Abstractions`

### Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `ExtractAsync` | Extracts text, page count, and metadata from a file stream |

### Properties

| Property | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| `SupportedExtensions` | Array of file extensions this extractor handles |

## Architecture

The document extractor sits in Sophon's document processing pipeline:

```
File Upload --> Type Detection --> IDocumentExtractor.ExtractAsync()
                                         |
                                   ExtractedDocument
                                    (text, pages, metadata)
                                         |
                              Chunking --> Embedding --> Index
                                         |
                              Summarization, Q&A, Search
```

## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- .NET 10 SDK
- `Sophon.Plugin.Abstractions` NuGet package

### Build

```bash
dotnet build
```

### Configuration

| Setting | Type | Required | Description |
|---------|------|----------|-------------|
| `maxFileSizeMb` | Number | No | Max file size in MB (default: 50) |

### Install

```bash
sophon plugins install ./{{Name}}.dll
```

## Development Guide

1. Update `SupportedExtensions` with the file extensions you want to handle
2. Implement the parsing logic in `ExtractAsync`
3. Extract all readable text content from the file format
4. Populate metadata (title, author, word count, etc.)
5. Test with various file sizes and edge cases (empty files, corrupted files)

### ExtractedDocument Fields

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `Text` | `string` | All extracted text content |
| `PageCount` | `int` | Number of pages (1 for non-paginated formats) |
| `Metadata` | `Dictionary<string, string>` | Key-value metadata pairs |

